\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x-5x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x+5x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(16x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(16x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)+\\frac{1}{32}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314960 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314960 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314960 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314960 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314960 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6c293fa-013e-59cd-b66e-3459611554eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314960 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha 