ratorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x+x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x-x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)]}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{20}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{20}(1-(-1))-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314962 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314962 #edb/ref 1069 "q-340492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314962 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314962 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314962 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11434a0f-ad34-5cb2-96ed-81af7783f37f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186314962 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the sum and differ